Third-party components, data, services and simulated integrations

Runtime: Node.js 24.x, including its bundled components under their respective licenses.
SQLite bundled with Node.js: public domain; https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html
Docker base: official node:24.13.0-bookworm-slim image; Debian components have their own licenses.

Runtime packages: Express (MIT), csv-parse (MIT), fast-xml-parser (MIT), Ajv (MIT), ajv-formats (MIT), jose (MIT), openid-client (MIT).
Development packages: TypeScript (Apache-2.0), tsx (MIT), DefinitelyTyped declarations (MIT).
Exact direct and transitive dependencies are recorded in package-lock.json.
License texts are supplied with installed packages. Python 3.12 runs the real company-context and ranking service; its locked dependencies are listed in requirements*.txt and requirements.lock. FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), jsonschema (MIT).

Data supplied by the hackathon organizers:
df_Uid_data_hack.csv, df_Uid_payment_hack.csv, df_Fid_Uid_link_hack.csv.
CSV inputs belong to their respective owners; verify data/README.md for the distinction between retained demo extracts and external organizer inputs. Dataset redistribution rights are not assumed.
Source: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Ep8wWoEHTg5Q8kwrLx2j_xFyxGUEVxFq

Bank research: nine Alfa-Bank documents supplied with the case.
research.json contains automatic OCR output, not an edited or endorsed bank publication.
Copyright remains with the respective authors. Original PDFs are linked, not bundled locally.
Source: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15xZTLF1lZ65p6o5xpNA_fRbxjoV-UlG1

Historical OCR preparation used PyMuPDF 1.26.6 (AGPL-3.0 or commercial license),
Tesseract OCR (Apache-2.0) and tessdata_fast Russian/English data (Apache-2.0).
These tools and binaries are not bundled or required by the Node.js application.
The old preprocessing utility is retained in the separate legacy backup.

LLMs: only the six permitted IDs listed in server/config.ts. Models are called via the
organizer gateway; no model weights are bundled. Live HTTP transport is implemented,
and a first live test confirmed gateway access. After fixes, a live analysis with tools and follow-up Q&A passed on a synthetic scenario. Semantic correctness across real cases remains unverified.

Offline simulated integrations: Alfa-Business UI shell, explicit development mode without authentication,
six synthetic seed news items, template analysis and Q&A in demo mode.
No internet-bank account, payment action or live banking API. Production supports a configured external OIDC identity provider; offline tests use an ephemeral HTTPS test authority, not real user accounts.
